   "id": "blockade",
   "title": "Blockade off the bay",
   "time": "12 September to 12 October",
   "narrative": "Navarino Bay, about five kilometres long and sheltered by the islet of Sphacteria, was the Ottoman navy's main base in the Peloponnese. Ibrahim Pasha's fleet, which left Alexandria on 5 August and joined other Ottoman ships there on 8 September, lay at anchor inside. Codrington arrived off the entrance on 12 September, talked with Ibrahim on 25 September and then withdrew to Zante, leaving a frigate to watch. Twice in early October he turned Ibrahim's sorties toward Patras back to port.",
