   "id": "gathering",
   "title": "The three squadrons meet",
   "time": "13 to 18 October",
   "narrative": "On 13 October the French squadron under Rigny and the Russian squadron under Van Heiden joined Codrington off Navarino. Behind the bay Ibrahim's troops were burning villages and fields, and a British landing party found Messinia close to famine. After futile attempts to reach Ibrahim, the three admirals met on 18 October and decided that a winter blockade was impracticable and that the population had to be protected. They resolved to anchor their ships face to face with the Ottoman fleet.",
