   "id": "prepare",
   "title": "Off the entrance",
   "time": "1:30 p.m., 20 October",
   "narrative": "Inside, the Ottoman-Egyptian fleet stood in a horseshoe plan devised by the French officer Letellier: three lines from Navarino fort round to the Sphacteria battery, ships of the line and large frigates in front, corvettes and brigs behind to fire through the gaps, fireships on the ends. Outside, Codrington signalled to prepare for action. Gun ports stayed half open and captains were ordered to fire only if attacked. The wind blew from the south-west, straight up the entrance.",
