   "id": "entry",
   "title": "The Allies sail in",
   "time": "About 2 p.m.",
   "narrative": "Codrington leads in Asia, the British ships followed by the French along the south-east side, closest to Navarino, and the Russians to port, abreast of the French but slightly behind. The shore batteries and the Ottoman corvettes at the mouth make no attempt to stop them through the southern channel, which was 1,500 m wide but only about 1,000 m usable because of rocks. A launch brings Ibrahim's protest. Codrington replies that he has come to give orders, not to receive them.",
