  {
   "id": "fireship",
   "title": "The fireship and the first shots",
   "time": "About 2:20 p.m.",
   "narrative": "At the mouth Captain Fellowes of Dartmouth, with two brigs and four schooners, was watching the corvettes and fireships on the Ottoman left. He saw a fireship being readied and sent a boat to make the crew desist. The Ottomans fired on the boat and lit the fireship. A cutter sent to tow it away was also fired on, and Fellowes had his men cover it with muskets. Sirene, entering at the tail of the line, joined in and an Ottoman corvette hit her with its guns.",
