  {
   "id": "french",
   "title": "The French on the Egyptian wing",
   "time": "About 2:30 p.m.",
   "narrative": "The chain reaction ran along the line within minutes. Scipion, behind Rigny's Sirene, was hit by Egyptian frigates on both sides, by the fort and by a fireship that jammed under her bowsprit and set her fore sails alight. Her crew went on firing while Trident took the fireship in tow with help from Dartmouth. Sirene fought a long duel with the 64-gun Ihsania until the Ottoman frigate blew up, then with Trident and Scipion silenced the fort.",
