  {
   "id": "centre",
   "title": "Asia in the centre",
   "time": "About 3 p.m.",
   "narrative": "Codrington's Asia lay between the Capitan Bey's flagship Fahti Bahri and Moharram Bey's frigate Guerriere. Moharram sent word that he would not attack, so Asia pounded the poorly manned Fahti Bahri. When Codrington's Greek interpreter was shot dead boarding Guerriere, she opened fire and was soon a burning wreck under the broadsides of Asia and Azov. Albion was pressed by all three Ottoman ships of the line until Breslaw left the French and came to her help.",
