   "title": "The first line is broken",
   "time": "About 4 p.m.",
   "narrative": "By around four o'clock all three Ottoman ships of the line and most of the large frigates of the front line were finished, and the fort and the Sphacteria battery were silent. The small British and French vessels under Dartmouth had kept the fireships away: apart from the attack on Scipion not one struck a target. The smaller craft of the second and third lines now lay open to Allied ships of the line, all of which were still fighting.",
