  {
   "id": "destruction",
   "title": "Destruction of the rear lines",
   "time": "4 to 6 p.m.",
   "narrative": "Codrington twice tried to order a ceasefire, but his signals vanished in the smoke or were ignored. Within two hours virtually the whole Ottoman fleet was destroyed, despite the bravery of its crews, which Codrington himself praised. Many dismasted hulks that could have been repaired were fired or blown up by their own crews to keep them from Allied hands, and men were trapped in the burning ships. Some had been shackled to their posts. Three quarters of the fleet was sunk.",
