  {
   "id": "aftermath",
   "title": "A shattered fleet",
   "time": "Dusk, 20 October",
   "narrative": "When the guns fell silent at dusk only eight of the 78 Ottoman and Egyptian vessels were seaworthy. Codrington reported 181 Allied dead and 480 wounded; Letellier gave about 3,000 Ottoman dead and 1,109 wounded, though Codrington thought the proportion might be reversed. Azov, Gangut and Iezekiil were disabled, the three British ships of the line had to go home for repair, and no Allied ship was sunk.",
